#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# log_barnes_g

#% text
# `log_barnes_g(z)` gives the logarithm of the Barnes G-function, analytic off the negative real axis.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# For `z > 0` it is the real `log(barnes_g(z))`; it does not overflow for large `z`, where `barnes_g` does.

#% item
# Machine numbers and balls give numerical values.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
log_barnes_g(5.0)
#% output
#= 2.4849066497880004

#% cell
log_barnes_g(0.5)
#% output
#= -0.5054330544896953

#% cell
log_barnes_g(1000.0)
#% output
#= 2698890.616533643

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# For a positive argument it agrees with `log(barnes_g(z))`:

#% cell
log_barnes_g(4.3) - log(barnes_g(4.3))
#% output
#= 0.0

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `barnes_g`, `log_gamma`
